The graph shows a cubic polynomial with leading coefficient $1$.
(a) Write its factored form with an unknown constant $k$.
(b) Find its equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},black]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->] (-3,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1)--(0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue,<->,domain=-2.5:3.5,samples=160,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.18*(\x+2)*(\x-2)*(\x-2)});
\draw (-2,0.08)--(-2,-0.08);
\draw (2,0.08)--(2,-0.08);
\path (-2,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-2$};
\path (2,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the equation of the degree-$5$ polynomial shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},black]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue,<->,domain=-2.8:2,samples=200,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-0.12*(\x+2)*(\x+2)*(\x-1)*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\draw (-2,0.08)--(-2,-0.08);
\draw (1,0.08)--(1,-0.08);
\path (-2,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-2$};
\path (1,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\fill (0,0.48) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0.48) node[above right] {$(0,12)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the equation of the cubic polynomial shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},black]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->] (-2,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2.5)--(0,2.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue,<->,domain=-1.2:3.5,samples=160,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.25*\x*\x*(\x-3)});
\draw (3,0.08)--(3,-0.08);
\path (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (0,0) node[above left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\fill (1,-0.5) circle (1.5pt);
\path (1,-0.5) node[below left] {$(1,-6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the equation of the quartic polynomial shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},black]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->] (-2,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3)--(0,1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue,<->,domain=-1.8:3.8,samples=180,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-0.1*(\x+1)*(\x+1)*(\x-3)*(\x-3)});
\draw (-1,0.08)--(-1,-0.08);
\draw (3,0.08)--(3,-0.08);
\path (-1,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-1$};
\path (3,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\fill (1,-1.6) circle (1.5pt);
\path (1,-1.6) node[below] {$(1,-32)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A crash barrier's depression is modelled by $d(t)=kt(t-a)^2$ for $0\leq t\leq8$, where $t$ is time in milliseconds and $d$ is depression in millimetres. The graph shows the barrier returning to its original position at $t=8$. At $t=2$, its depression is $18$ mm.
Find $a$, explain its meaning, and find the equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},black]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->] (-0.4,0)--(9,0) node[right] {$t\,(\mathrm{ms})$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.4)--(0,3) node[above] {$d\,(\mathrm{mm})$};
\draw[thick,curveblue,domain=0:8,samples=160,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.1*0.25*\x*(\x-8)*(\x-8)});
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (8,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\path (8,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$8$};
\fill (2,1.8) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,1.8) node[above left] {$(2,18)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which equation could represent the quartic graph?
A. $y=(x+1)(x-2)^3$
B. $y=(x-1)(2+x)^3$
C. $y=(x+1)(2-x)^3$
D. $y=(x+1)^3(2-x)$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},black]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->] (-2,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2.5)--(0,2.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue,<->,domain=-1.4:3.6,samples=200,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.12*(\x+1)*(2-\x)*(2-\x)*(2-\x)});
\draw (-1,0.08)--(-1,-0.08);
\draw (2,0.08)--(2,-0.08);
\path (-1,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-1$};
\path (2,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
